@* Card shell for a chart or data panel: heading + optional toolbar, then the
   loading → error → empty → content ladder.

   That ladder was written out three times (AllReposComparisonChart, ContributorChart,
   RepositoryDetail), ~40 near-identical lines each, along with three copies of the
   `.arc-*` / `.cc-*` / `.rd-*` styles that dressed it.

   Rooted at a plain <div> on purpose: Blazor's `::deep` compiles to `[b-scope] .x` and needs a
   plain HTML ancestor carrying the scope id. Rooting at <RadzenCard> would leave nothing in this
   file carrying the id, and every rule in ChartCard.razor.css would silently match nothing. *@

@* Do NOT put `content-visibility: auto` on this card. It was tried (as a `u-defer-paint`
   utility, since deleted) and reverted.

   A RadzenChart sizes its own <svg> by measuring the element it is mounted in. Under
   `content-visibility: auto` an off-screen subtree skips layout, so that measurement returns the
   `contain-intrinsic-size` placeholder instead of real geometry — and the chart draws to the
   placeholder, or draws nothing at all. On the repository detail page, which stacks several
   charts so the lower ones start below the fold, this took out the extension donut entirely and
   broke the mobile no-horizontal-overflow guarantee (Detail_ExtensionBreakdownRendersADonut,
   Detail_MobileDoesNotScrollHorizontally, Detail_MobileTapTargetsAreLargeEnough).

   It is simply wrong for anything that measures itself in JS.

   u-glass sits on the surface rather than the wrapper so the blur and the shadow read as one
   surface, not a plain div wrapping a styled card. *@
<div class="chart-card">
    <RadzenCard class="chart-card__surface u-glass">
        <RadzenStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal"
                     AlignItems="AlignItems.Center"
                     JustifyContent="JustifyContent.SpaceBetween"
                     Wrap="FlexWrap.Wrap"
                     Gap="0.5rem"
                     class="chart-card__toolbar">
            <RadzenStack Gap="0.15rem" class="chart-card__heading">
                <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.H6" class="chart-card__title">@Title</RadzenText>
                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(Description))
                {
                    <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption" class="chart-card__description">@Description</RadzenText>
                }
            </RadzenStack>

            @if (Toolbar is not null)
            {
                <div class="chart-card__actions">@Toolbar</div>
            }
        </RadzenStack>

        @if (IsLoading)
        {
            <RadzenSkeleton Width="100%" class="chart-card__skeleton" />
        }
        else if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(ErrorMessage))
        {
            <RadzenAlert AlertStyle="AlertStyle.Warning" ShowIcon="true" AllowClose="false">
                @ErrorMessage
                @if (OnRetry.HasDelegate)
                {
                    <RadzenButton Text="Retry" Icon="refresh" Size="ButtonSize.Small" Variant="Variant.Text"
                                  Click="@OnRetry" class="chart-card__retry" />
                }
            </RadzenAlert>
        }
        else if (IsEmpty)
        {
            <RadzenStack AlignItems="AlignItems.Center" Gap="0.35rem" class="chart-card__empty">
                <RadzenIcon Icon="@EmptyIcon" class="chart-card__empty-icon" />
                <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Body1" class="chart-card__empty-text">@EmptyText</RadzenText>
                @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(EmptyHint))
                {
                    <RadzenText TextStyle="TextStyle.Caption" class="chart-card__empty-hint">@EmptyHint</RadzenText>
                }
            </RadzenStack>
        }
        else
        {
            @* Fades and settles in the first time real content replaces the skeleton/empty state.
               Transform/opacity only, so it cannot affect the RadzenChart sizing measurement the
               comment above warns about — the wrapper is a plain block, present with real
               dimensions for the whole animation, never `content-visibility`-skipped. *@
            <div class="chart-card__content u-enter">
                @ChildContent
            </div>
        }
    </RadzenCard>
</div>

@code {
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public string Title { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    [Parameter] public string? Description { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Controls rendered on the right of the heading — typically a ChartRangeSelector.</summary>
    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? Toolbar { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public bool IsLoading { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string? ErrorMessage { get; set; }

    /// <summary>Wired to the retry button; the button is omitted when no handler is supplied.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback OnRetry { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public bool IsEmpty { get; set; }
    [Parameter] public string EmptyIcon { get; set; } = "bar_chart";
    [Parameter] public string EmptyText { get; set; } = "No data yet.";
    [Parameter] public string? EmptyHint { get; set; }

    [Parameter] public RenderFragment? ChildContent { get; set; }
}
